<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.7.1: Evaluating Variable Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02443</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.7.1: Evaluating Variable Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>41c4b1bc-59bb-4b49-9c13-827b2a3ac0bf</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Evaluate each expression for \(a=9\), \(b=-5\), and \(c=-2\).</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise id="_2ce28f30-9311-45ec-8259-4a441abd6f6b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the value of \(-b\).</para><para>\(-b\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-(-5)=5\)</para><para>The correct answer is 5: \(-(-5)=5\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_713726b7-cb7a-440b-a5cc-d66fcd5df6d2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the value of \(b^2\).</para><para>\(b^2\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((-5)^2=25\)</para><para>The correct answer is 25: \((-5)^2=25\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_3959ab64-2000-442d-9e18-4ab69756c335" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the value of \(b^2−4ac\).</para><para>\(b^2−4ac\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \((-5)^2−4(9)(-2)=25-(36)(-2)=25-(-72)=25+72=97\)</para><para>The correct answer is 97: \((-5)^2−4(9)(-2)=25-(36)(-2)=25-(-72)=25+72=97\).</para></solution></exercise></section>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_7335966d-dc58-4542-a715-339e24f82cd1" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> answers for \(-b \pm \sqrt{a}\).</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(-(-5)+\sqrt{9}=5+3=8\) and \(-(-5)-\sqrt{9}=5-3=2\)</para><para>The correct answers are 2 and 8: \(-(-5)+\sqrt{9}=5+3=8\) and \(-(-5)-\sqrt{9}=5-3=2\)</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
